__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Local run artifacts. The state DB is committed on purpose once real runs
# start (it is the archive + dedupe memory) — see README.
site/preview/
.env

# Generated issues were ignored through v0-v2 so locally-built pages — which
# come from SYNTHETIC fixtures — could not be published as real reef news.
# v3 commits them from the Action instead, because Pages replaces the whole
# site on every deploy and an uncommitted permalink 404s a week later.
#
# The protection that replaced the ignore is the publish gate in daily.yml: a
# partial run never commits, and --offline never runs in CI at all. Do not
# `git add site/index.html` by hand from a local --offline build.

# Run markers. Written by `daily-dive run` so the workflow can tell "this run
# built a page" from "a page was already committed here", and "the send failed"
# from "the issue failed". Never committed — they describe one run, not state.
.run-built
.send-failed
